# 32. Architecture Principles

Follow these principles:

### Security by Design

Security must be part of the architecture rather than an afterthought.

### Zero Trust

Never implicitly trust users, services, scanners, or uploaded artifacts.

### Least Privilege

Every service and user should receive only the permissions required.

### Modular Architecture

Every security engine should be independently replaceable or upgradeable.

### Single Source of Truth

Avoid duplicate or contradictory security metrics.

### Evidence-Based Findings

Security findings must be backed by evidence.

### No Fake Data

Do not generate fake vulnerabilities, metrics, scan results, or risk scores to make the UI look populated.

For development, clearly separate:

```text
Mock/Test Data
```

from:

```text
Production Data
```

