# 41. Critical Development Rules

Before implementing any feature:

1. Inspect the existing architecture.
2. Identify dependencies.
3. Determine where the feature belongs.
4. Avoid duplicating existing functionality.
5. Reuse existing components and services.
6. Maintain a single source of truth.
7. Maintain strict type safety.
8. Do not break existing functionality.
9. Add appropriate tests.
10. Verify the feature end-to-end.

Do not create temporary hacks that become permanent architecture.

Do not hide errors.

Do not silently swallow scanner failures.

If a scanner fails, display:

```text
Scanner Status: Failed
Reason: <actual reason>
```

rather than presenting an artificial successful result.

